        { "text": "$2\\sqrt{3x+8}+C$", "why": "Divided by the coefficient $a=3$ but not by the new power $\\dfrac{1}{2}$." },
        { "text": "$-\\dfrac{9}{\\sqrt{(3x+8)^{3}}}$", "why": "Differentiated $6(3x+8)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}$ instead of finding its primitive." }
      ],
      "solution_text": "$\\dfrac{6}{\\sqrt{3x+8}}$\n$=6(3x+8)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}$\n$\\displaystyle\\int 6(3x+8)^{-\\frac{1}{2}}\\,dx=\\dfrac{6(3x+8)^{\\frac{1}{2}}}{3\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)}+C$\n$=4\\sqrt{3x+8}+C$"
    }
